      "note": "The sequence of triangles, three squares, twelve-pointed star, the six fish, the diagonals and the two stars of parallel lines follows this tutorial.",
      "steps": [6, 7, 8, 9, 10]
    }
  ],
  "given": {
    "O": "The centre of the window's rosette.",
    "A": "Any point to the right of O. The distance OA is the radius of the first circle, and the unit for every length."
  },
  "steps": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "text": "Draw a horizontal line, put the compass point on it and draw a circle. Keep the compass at this opening until the end.",
      "create": {"h": {"line": {"through": ["O", "A"]}}, "c": {"circle": {"centre": "O", "through": "A"}}},
      "animate": "compass"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Put the compass point where the circle crosses the line on the right and draw a circle through the centre. Do the same on the left. The two new circles touch at the centre.",
      "create": {
        "E": {"point": {"meet": ["c", "h"], "pick": {"angle": 0}}},
        "W": {"point": {"meet": ["c", "h"], "pick": {"angle": 180}}},
        "cE": {"circle": {"centre": "E", "radiusOf": "c"}},
        "cW": {"circle": {"centre": "W", "radiusOf": "c"}}
      },
      "highlight": ["c", "h"],
      "animate": "compass"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The two new circles cross the first one at four more points. Draw a circle of the same size around each of them. Six circles now ring the first, and their crossings divide it into six.",
      "create": {
        "P60": {"point": {"meet": ["c", "cE"], "pick": {"angle": 60}}},
        "P300": {"point": {"meet": ["c", "cE"], "pick": {"angle": 300}}},
        "P120": {"point": {"meet": ["c", "cW"], "pick": {"angle": 120}}},
        "P240": {"point": {"meet": ["c", "cW"], "pick": {"angle": 240}}},
        "c60": {"circle": {"centre": "P60", "radiusOf": "c"}},
        "c120": {"circle": {"centre": "P120", "radiusOf": "c"}},
        "c240": {"circle": {"centre": "P240", "radiusOf": "c"}},
        "c300": {"circle": {"centre": "P300", "radiusOf": "c"}}
      },
      "highlight": ["cE", "cW"],
      "animate": "compass"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Outside the first circle, each pair of neighbouring circles makes a large petal. Rule a line through the centre and the tips of two opposite petals; do it three times. One line is vertical and two lean at 30° either side of it.",
      "create": {
        "X30": {"point": {"meet": ["cE", "c60"], "pick": {"farthest": "O"}}},
        "X90": {"point": {"meet": ["c60", "c120"], "pick": {"farthest": "O"}}},
        "X150": {"point": {"meet": ["c120", "cW"], "pick": {"farthest": "O"}}},
        "m30": {"line": {"through": ["O", "X30"]}},
        "m90": {"line": {"through": ["O", "X90"]}},
        "m150": {"line": {"through": ["O", "X150"]}}
      },
      "highlight": ["cE", "c60", "c120", "cW"],
      "animate": "ruler"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The three lines cut the circle at six more points. With the six points from the circles, the circle is now divided into twelve, one point every 30°. Join every other point, starting at the top, to draw a hexagon standing on a corner.",
      "create": {
        "D30": {"point": {"meet": ["c", "m30"], "pick": {"angle": 30}}},
        "D90": {"point": {"meet": ["c", "m90"], "pick": {"angle": 90}}},
        "D150": {"point": {"meet": ["c", "m150"], "pick": {"angle": 150}}},
        "D210": {"point": {"meet": ["c", "m30"], "pick": {"angle": 210}}},
        "D270": {"point": {"meet": ["c", "m90"], "pick": {"angle": 270}}},
        "D330": {"point": {"meet": ["c", "m150"], "pick": {"angle": 330}}},
        "hex": {"polygon": ["D30", "D90", "D150", "D210", "D270", "D330"]},
        "flat": {"polygon": ["E", "P60", "P120", "W", "P240", "P300"]}
      },
      "highlight": ["m30", "m90", "m150"],
      "animate": "ruler"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Join the top point to the points four places round on either side, and close the triangle. Do the same from the bottom point. The two triangles make a six-pointed star inside the hexagon.",
      "create": {"up": {"polygon": ["D90", "D330", "D210"]}, "down": {"polygon": ["D30", "D270", "D150"]}},
      "highlight": ["D30", "D90", "D150", "D210", "D270", "D330"],
      "animate": "ruler"
    },
    {
      "id": 7,
      "text": "Draw three squares, each through four points three places apart: one standing on the horizontal, and two turned 30° either way.",
      "create": {
        "sqA": {"polygon": ["D90", "E", "D270", "W"]},
        "sqB": {"polygon": ["P60", "D330", "P240", "D150"]},
        "sqC": {"polygon": ["D30", "P300", "D210", "P120"]}
      },
      "highlight": ["E", "D30", "P60", "D90", "P120", "D150", "W", "D210", "P240", "D270", "P300", "D330"],
      "animate": "ruler"
    },
    {
      "id": 8,
      "text": "Draw a twelve-pointed star: from each point rule a line to the point five places round, so that the lines go round the circle twice before closing. Carry each line on across the drawing.",
      "create": {
        "st75": {"line": {"through": ["E", "D150"]}},
        "st105": {"line": {"through": ["D30", "W"]}},
        "st135": {"line": {"through": ["P60", "D210"]}},
        "st165": {"line": {"through": ["D90", "P240"]}},
        "st195": {"line": {"through": ["P120", "D270"]}},
        "st225": {"line": {"through": ["D150", "P300"]}},
        "st255": {"line": {"through": ["W", "D330"]}},
        "st285": {"line": {"through": ["D210", "E"]}},
        "st315": {"line": {"through": ["P240", "D30"]}},
        "st345": {"line": {"through": ["D270", "P60"]}},
        "st15": {"line": {"through": ["P300", "D90"]}},
        "st45": {"line": {"through": ["D330", "P120"]}}
      },
      "highlight": ["E", "D30", "P60", "D90", "P120", "D150", "W", "D210", "P240", "D270", "P300", "D330"],
      "animate": "ruler"
    },
    {
      "id": 9,
      "text": "Now the six fish, one at each of the points on the horizontal and the lines at 60°. The fish's nose is the point on the circle, and its fins run back along the two square sides from the nose until they meet the triangles. Its tail is a cross: where two other squares cross on the line through the nose, rule a line to each place where the nose's square cuts the hexagon, and carry both lines on until they meet the triangles.",
